- `branch(b1, XOR)`, `branch(b2, XOR)`, `branch(b3, XOR)`: Missing `guard` statements to encode the explicit decision criteria stated in the description ("If the inventory level is above/below the minimum", "If the purchase order is rejected/accepted"), leaving the choice logic semantically unspecified.
- `branch(b2, XOR)`: Incorrectly enforces mutual exclusion for steps that are explicitly concurrent in the source ("At the same time, complete the following steps: reserve funds for the purchase and send the purchase order to the supplier"), which requires parallel/AND routing rather than XOR.
- `branch(b3, XOR)` & missing `precedence(b3, ...)`: Omits the required feedback loop described as "After reworking the purchase order, review it again," leaving `b3` structurally isolated and breaking the intended process progression.
- `action(n9, "reserve funds and send PO")` and `action(n12, "send to supplier")`: Misrepresents concurrent tasks as separate, mutually exclusive alternatives; the source treats "reserve funds" and "send the purchase order" as simultaneous post-acceptance actions, but the model splits them across distinct XOR paths.
- `end(e2)` and `end(e3)`: Fragments a single concluding phase into two disjoint terminations; the description specifies one unified endpoint ("Once the packing slip is received, release the reserved funds and then the process ends"), whereas the model prematurely closes via two separate flows originating from the misconfigured `b2` branch.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b3` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: branch(b3,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n5` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n7` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n9` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n12` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S4] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: b3, n7, n8 | DSL: branch(b3,XOR); action(n7,"rework: purchase order"); action(n8,"review: purchase order")